# AT templates — '## group' starts a section, a '# description' line describes
# the command below it, and the command line is sent to the modem as-is.
# '#' lines are never sent. Full help is in generic.user. Edit freely.
#
# Sierra Wireless EM7345 and other Intel XMM7160 (FIH7160) modules. The module
# is labelled Sierra, but the chip is Intel: the Sierra '!' commands
# (AT!ENTERCND, AT!BAND, AT!IMPREF) always answer ERROR here.
# The XMM commands below are taken from the related XMM7360 (Fibocom L850/L860)
# and are NOT confirmed on the 7160 — an ERROR in reply is normal and harmless.
# Everything that is guaranteed to work (ATI, +CSQ, +CESQ, +COPS, +CEREG,
# +CGMI/+CGMM/+CGMR, +CGDCONT) lives in generic.user.

## Cell and signal

# Serving and neighbour cells
AT+XMCI=1

# Extended signal quality (Intel)
AT+XCESQ?

# Cell change info
AT+XCCINFO?

# Aggregation (CA) — the 7160 is Cat 4, aggregation is not expected
AT+XLEC?

## Bands and modes

# Network mode and bands
AT+XACT?

# Supported modes and bands
AT+XACT=?
